.TH CGMAHJONG 6 "November 2026" "cggames 1.4.0"
.SH NAME
cgmahjong \- the tile matching game
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cgmahjong
.RI [ "toolkit options" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cgmahjong
is a solitaire game played with mahjong tiles stacked in layers.
Take the tiles off the board in pairs: two tiles match when they show
the same face, and a tile can be taken when no tile lies on top of it
and it is free on its left or its right side.
The game is won when every tile has been taken, and every game dealt
can be won.
.PP
Click a free tile to select it, then click its match.
A tile that doesn't match is selected in place of the first, and
clicking the selected tile again lets it go.
.PP
.B Hint
makes a pair that can be taken blink, at a cost of 30 seconds: the
selected tile's match, if it has one free.
When no pair can be taken, the game offers to shuffle the tiles left
into new places, at a cost of 60 seconds and forgetting the moves made
before, to start a new game, or to take the last move back.
.B Pause
hides the faces and stops the clock.
.PP
Each game has a number, which
.B New Game with Seed
shows and takes, so a game can be played again, here or on another
computer.
.PP
There are nine maps to lay the tiles out in, chosen in the
preferences: Easy, The Ziggurat, Four Bridges, Cloud, Tic-Tac-Toe,
Red Dragon, Pyramid's Walls, Confounding Cross and Difficult.
The ten best times on each map are kept.
.PP
The tiles are drawn to fill the window, as large as it is made, and the
board's size is kept for next time.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cggames/cgmahjong.conf
The preferences.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/cggames/cgmahjong.scores
The best times.
.PP
Without the variables,
.I ~/.config
and
.I ~/.local/share
are used.
.TP
.I PREFIX/share/cggames/cgmahjong/layouts.map
The maps after Easy, which is built in.
.TP
.I PREFIX/share/cggames/cgmahjong/tiles
The pictures on the tiles' faces, all in one SVG,
.IR tiles.svg ;
the tiles themselves are drawn by the game, at the size the window
calls for and as sharp as the screen allows.
.SH AUTHORS
cgmahjong is GNOME Mahjongg from gnome-games 1.4, ported to CGTK.
Francisco Bustamante, Max Watson, Heinz Hempe, Michael Meeks and
Philippe Chavin wrote GNOME Mahjongg.
The maps after Easy and Difficult come from GNOME Mahjongg 2.32, which
credits its maps to Rexford Newbould and Krzysztof Foltman.
The faces are now public domain riichi tiles, with flowers and seasons
drawn for them.
